\pard\sa180\sl280\slmult1\f1\fs40 READ ME FIRST\par
\pard\sa240\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs26\cf2 The Pastor Bible, on your Mac. Please read this before you double-click anything.\par
\pard\sa120\sl300\slmult1\f1\fs30\cf1 Putting it on your Mac\par
\pard\sa100\sl300\slmult1\f0\fs26 1.\tab Drag The Pastor Bible onto the Applications folder in this window.\par
2.\tab Open your Applications folder and double-click The Pastor Bible.\par
3.\tab Your Mac will stop you. That is expected, and the next section says exactly what to do.\par
\pard\sa120\sl300\slmult1\f1\fs30 Why your Mac stops you\par
\pard\sa180\sl300\slmult1\f0\fs26 This is a free project and nobody has paid Apple's yearly developer fee, so macOS has no company name to show you and refuses to open the app the first time.\par
\pard\sa180\sl300\slmult1 The program is not damaged and there is nothing wrong with your Mac. The exact checksum of the file you downloaded is published on the release page, so you can check for yourself that what you have is what we published.\par
\pard\sa120\sl300\slmult1\f1\fs30 If your Mac runs macOS 15 (Sequoia) or newer\par
\pard\sa100\sl300\slmult1\f0\fs26 1.\tab Double-click The Pastor Bible. A message appears saying it cannot be opened.\par
2.\tab Click Done.\par
3.\tab Open the Apple menu, then System Settings, then Privacy & Security.\par
4.\tab Scroll down. There is a line about The Pastor Bible with an Open Anyway button beside it. Click it.\par
5.\tab Confirm with your password or Touch ID, then click Open.\par
\pard\sa120\sl300\slmult1\f1\fs30 If your Mac runs macOS 13 (Ventura) or macOS 14 (Sonoma)\par
\pard\sa100\sl300\slmult1\f0\fs26 1.\tab Find The Pastor Bible in your Applications folder. Do not use Launchpad for this.\par
2.\tab Hold the Control key and click it, then choose Open from the menu that appears.\par
3.\tab Click Open in the box that appears.\par
\pard\sa180\sl300\slmult1\cf2 On these versions, Privacy & Security also has an Open Anyway button for about an hour after you first try.\par
\pard\sa180\sl300\slmult1\f1\cf1 You only do this once.\f0  After that it opens by double-clicking, like anything else on your Mac.\par
\pard\sa180\sl300\slmult1 Not sure which version you have? Apple menu, then About This Mac.\par
\pard\sa120\sl300\slmult1\f1\fs30 The first time you open it\par
\pard\sa180\sl300\slmult1\f0\fs26 It downloads one file, about 4.7 GB: the part that writes the answers. That is the only time this program uses the internet. Then it offers to check itself, which takes a few minutes on a laptop. Neither of those has stopped working; both are meant to take a while.\par
\pard\sa180\sl300\slmult1 On an Intel Mac there is no graphics card this program can use, so answers take several minutes. The smaller model, in Settings, is faster.\par
\pard\sa120\sl300\slmult1\f1\fs30 Before you use it\par
\pard\sa180\sl300\slmult1\f0\fs26 The Pastor Bible is a study tool. It is not a substitute for a pastor, a physician or a counsellor, and it does not take sides between traditions.\par
\pard\sa180\sl300\slmult1\f1 If you are thinking of harming yourself or someone else, please contact your local emergency number or a crisis line now.\f0  The full disclaimer and the crisis note are on the first screen of the app and at the top of the README on the release page.\par
\pard\sa180\sl300\slmult1\fs22\cf2 These steps are Apple's own, written down from Apple's documentation on 1 September 2026. Nobody has yet walked through them on a real Mac with this app. If what you see does not match what is written here, please tell us: that report is a gift.\par
}
